#, no-c-format
msgid "Using &parley;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:184
#, no-c-format
msgid "Overview"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:186
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This is the main window of &parley;. It consists of two areas: the lesson "
"list in the left third of the window and the current vocabulary list in the "
"other two thirds."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:192 index.docbook:234
#, no-c-format
msgid "Screenshot"
msgstr "Ecran"

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:198
#, no-c-format
msgid "The lesson list"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:199
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The lesson list on the left shows all lessons in your vocabulary file. If "
"you mark a lesson, is will become the current one. In this case it is "
"survival training."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:200
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The ticked box left of the name of each lesson indicates that it is to be "
"included in the practice. You may choose as many lessons for a test as you "
"like."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:201
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"On top of the list there is a combo box which allows you to select which "
"vocabulary selection you want displayed on the right:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:203
#, no-c-format
msgid "The current lesson only (survival training in this case)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:204
#, no-c-format
msgid "Lessons in the test (the ones with a checkmark)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:205
#, no-c-format
msgid "All lessons (everything in the vocabulary file)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:211
#, no-c-format
msgid "The vocabulary list"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:212
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Depending on your selection, one or more lessons are displayed on the right "
"side of the screen."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:215
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A green check mark in the second column means that this entry is active. A "
"red and white \"X\" indicates a deactivated entry that will not be "
"practiced. See Editing Entries for more information on active entries."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:217
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you mark a range of entries to work with, their background colour "
"changes. Many editing functions work for multiple entries simultaneously."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:219
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The colour in the column with the original will vary if you have two or more "
"columns with translations. If the cursor is in one of the translations the "
"colour represents its grade <quote>to the original</quote>. See section "
"<link linkend=\"general-settings\">entry dialog</link> for more on this."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:228
#, no-c-format
msgid "The search bar"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:229
#, no-c-format
msgid "The search bar is located above the vocabulary table."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:230
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can use the search bar to filter your vocabulary. If you type in a "
"string, you will only see entries with this string in the vocabulary table."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:240
#, no-c-format
msgid "The status bar"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:241
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The status bar is located at the bottom of the main window. It is empty at "
"the moment."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:247
#, no-c-format
msgid "Available file formats"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:249
#, no-c-format
msgid "&parley; can read and write the following file formats:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:252
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"its native xml-style document type with the extension <literal role="
"\"extension\">.kvtml</literal>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:255
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you want to share documents with others, use this format as it is the "
"only file format that is capable of storing <emphasis>all</emphasis> "
"properties in &parley;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:260
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"simple text files with special delimiters between the entries which are also "
"used by simple database programs. The extension is <literal role=\"extension"
"\">.csv</literal> in this case."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:265
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"There are a lot of files on the Internet which use the tab stops or one or "
"two colons to separate the languages. To select this separator use the tab "
"for setting the <link linkend=\"general-settings\"><guilabel> Copy &amp; "
"Paste</guilabel> options</link> in the <guimenu>Settings</guimenu> "
"<guimenuitem>Configure &parley;...</guimenuitem> dialog."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:270
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&parley; reads the first few bytes of a file and guesses its file format. If "
"none of the special types like <literal role=\"extension\">.kvtml</literal> "
"or <literal role=\"extension\">.lex</literal> are recognized, it will try "
"the <literal role=\"extension\">.csv</literal> format."
msgstr ""

