#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:416
#, no-c-format
msgid "How should I learn?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:418
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The usual way to learn with &parley; is to use one of its practice modes."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:420
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"It keeps track of your knowledge of the expressions by assigning them to one "
"of seven levels ranging from <quote>Level 1</quote> to <quote>Level 7</"
"quote>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:424
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Several options are implemented which can be configured in the dialogue for "
"the practice options."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:428
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To keep the amount of expressions in a query in a reasonable range, you may "
"restrict it to one lesson and/or a certain word type. Research in psychology "
"of learning suggests that the number of entries in one lesson should not "
"exceed about 30."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:431
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The range of a query can depend on the current grade, the number of queries "
"and the last query date."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:433
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Learning is efficient if you repeat new vocabulary in growing intervals. "
"There is a blocking and expiring mechanism for that case, so that you are "
"not obliged to modify the settings after each cycle. Correctly answered "
"expressions are blocked at least for the given time and will only be shown "
"after the period of time defined as expiration time."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:436
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"For your personal taste or just for becoming acquainted with a new word, you "
"may choose a query that shows the solution together with several other "
"randomly chosen words. This is called multiple choice query."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:441
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Special word types need special queries. For this reason there are queries "
"for the conjugation of verbs, comparison form of adjectives and the articles "
"of nouns."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:444
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When querying, &parley; shows the expressions in random order until you "
"confirm all as <quote>known</quote>. If you did not select a special lesson, "
"all lessons are queried one after the other."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:448
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When you leave &parley;, expressions left in a running query are stored "
"accordingly. At a later restart you can resume the query (this does not "
"apply to special queries with verbs, articles and comparisons at the "
"moment). Those expressions are marked with a green check mark in the <link "
"linkend=\"overview\">main view</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:456
#, no-c-format
msgid "Sharing files and downloading dictionaries"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:459
#, no-c-format
msgid "Contributing your files to &parley;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:461
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you have created a kvtml file, please send an email to &Anne-Marie."
"Mahfouf.mail; with the file attached and I will put the file in the <ulink "
"url=\"http://edu.kde.org/contrib/kvtml.php\">contributed kvtml files</ulink> "
"on <ulink url=\"http://edu.kde.org\">the &kde;-Edu website</ulink> so other "
"people will be able to use it."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:464
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you modify existing files or create new files based on copyrighted "
"material you must ask the author for permission. Even taking literal "
"examples from schoolbooks might be problematic! The files must be licensed "
"under a free license, please indicate it in your mail when you send the file."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:472
#, no-c-format
msgid "Downloading and installing existing files"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:474
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&parley; is shipped with only two examples files. But you can easily get and "
"install existing files using the <menuchoice><guimenu>File</guimenu> "
"<guimenuitem>Get New Vocabularies...</guimenuitem> </menuchoice> menu, "
"provided you have an Internet connection. The following dialog is then "
"displayed:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:477
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>Get New Vocabularies... dialog</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:480
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>Get New Vocabularies... dialog</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:484
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Choose the file you want to get. The <guibutton>Details</guibutton> button "
"will give you more details about the content of the highlighted file. Click "
"the <guibutton>Install</guibutton> button. The file is then downloaded from "
"its location on the Internet, saved on your hard disk and opened in &parley; "
"current window."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:487
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The files you download are saved in your home folder in the "
"<filename>Vocabularies</filename> folder."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:491
#, no-c-format
msgid "Other dictionaries on the web"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:494
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you are German an want to learn English (or vice versa) you can download "
"the monthly vocabulary list provided by the German magazine <ulink url="
"\"http://www.spotlight-online.de\">Spotlight-Online</ulink>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:497
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The &parley; distribution contains an executable called "
"<command>spotlight2kvtml</command> to transform those lists in kvtml format. "
"The original files come as &Windows; Word DOC-files so you have to save them "
"as ANSI-TXT files before starting conversion. <application>StarOffice</"
"application> or <application>kword</application> can do this job."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:503
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<command>spotlight2kvtml</command> needs the 3 parameters "
"<parameter>filename</parameter>, <parameter>month</parameter> and "
"<parameter>year</parameter> and produces a file in the same folder with the "
"same name and the extension <literal role=\"extension\">kvtml</literal>:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: userinput
#: index.docbook:507
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<command>spotlight2kvtml</command> <replaceable>0199.txt 01 99</replaceable>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:511
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Thanks to a contribution by Andreas Neuper you can download files from "
"<ulink url=\"http://www.vokabeln.de/files.htm\">Langenscheidt</ulink>. This "
"is a german site and contains files in several languages. This distribution "
"contains his perl script <command>langen2kvtml</command> to transform those "
"lists in kvtml format."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:519
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<command>langen2kvtml</command> needs only the original filename as "
"parameter and tries to extract as much information as possible from the "
"source file. For example is keeps the lesson names, conjugations and "
"articles."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:523
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"It produces a file in the same folder with the same name and the extension "
"<literal role=\"extension\">kvtml</literal>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:527
#, no-c-format
msgid "Files in kvtml format are available at:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: ulink
#: index.docbook:531
#, no-c-format
msgid "&kde;-Edu Contributed Learning Files"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:537
#, no-c-format
msgid "Dictionaries in ascii-format are for example available at:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:540
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<ulink url=\"ftp://ftp.gwdg.de/pub/misc/dictionary/english/words.gz\">ftp."
"gwdg.d e/pub/misc/dictionary/english/words.gz</ulink> (approx. 1035 kB)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:548
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Dictionaries from the <ulink url=\"http://www3.futureware.at/kquick.htm"
"\">*Quick project</ulink> in <quote>CSV</quote> format but encoded in "
"<quote>UTF8</quote> so you should have all characters rendered correctly. "
"The files are available from its <ulink url=\"http://www3.futureware.at/1dim."
"htm\">download section</ulink>. They are in compressed &Windows; <literal "
"role=\"extension\">.EXE</literal> format so you have to use "
"<application>unzip</application> to extract the files."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:560
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you know another source please tell <ulink url=\"mailto:annma@kde.org"
"\">me</ulink> to include it here."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:566
#, no-c-format
msgid "Translator applications"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:568
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you do not want to learn but just need quick translations of expressions "
"in larger dictionaries you might be unhappy with &parley; if your computer "
"doesn't have much memory and MHz. A 150000 entry file consumes about 60M and "
"takes ages to load if your system is short of memory."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:573
#, no-c-format
msgid "In this case you might want to try one of the following:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:575
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<ulink url=\"http://www.franken.de/users/duffy1/rjakob/\">kdsing</ulink> "
"(&kde;)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:580
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<ulink url=\"http://www.tm.informatik.uni-frankfurt.de/~razi/steak/steak.html"
"\"> steak/xsteak</ulink> (console/X)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:586
#, no-c-format
msgid "<ulink url=\"http://dict.tu-chemnitz.de/\">Ding</ulink> (TCL)."
msgstr ""

